 (persistent NAND boot)

OpenWrt installed and running persistently from NAND on real hardware.
Two hardware-found fixes unlocked it: FIT config named config@hk07 (OEM
bootipq board-name lookup) and single-slot install to slot 0 (the
'rootfs' partition OpenWrt's root-mount targets). Eth/WiFi(WPA2)/overlay
and reboot-persistence all validated. Update status: resolved items,
install method, single-slot recovery.
